# CLI-triggered `vercel deploy` uploads from the repo root do not reliably
# respect .gitignore (confirmed 2026-08-23: swept in 15,782 files vs. the
# 3,367 git actually tracks). This restricts the upload to what the
# dcs build (installCommand/buildCommand in sites/dcs/vercel.json) needs:
# workspace source under sites/ and packages/, plus root manifests/config.
# The Vercel-side installCommand reinstalls all deps itself, so none of
# this repo's local node_modules or caches need to travel.
#
# `.git` is deliberately NOT excluded here, even though it's ~266MB. Every
# site's ignoreCommand (`npx turbo-ignore <site> --fallback=HEAD^1`) needs a
# real `.git` directory to diff against — .vercelignore is applied to every
# build's clone (git-push-triggered included), not just CLI deploys, before
# ignoreCommand runs. With `.git` excluded, turbo-ignore's `--dry=json` call
# failed with "Unable to query SCM: not a Git repository" on literally every
# push, and turbo-ignore fails OPEN on any error — so every project rebuilt
# unconditionally on every push to every branch from 2026-08-23 onward, no
# matter what changed. Confirmed via live build logs (see PR #74's deploys)
# before restoring this. The occasional oversized CLI-triggered upload is a
# far cheaper trade-off than an unconditional full-monorepo rebuild on every
# single push.

node_modules
.turbo
.next
output
local-business-platform_venv
playwright-report
test-results
.claude
.agents
.code-review-graph
tasks
supabase
*.tsbuildinfo

# `*.png` is deliberately NOT listed here. It matched 17 git-TRACKED files that
# live inside site package directories (colossus-scaffolding's 12 Playwright
# visual baselines, sites/dcs/public/social-share.png, and the npracing v1/v3
# app/icon.png + app/apple-icon.png). .vercelignore is applied to the build's
# working tree before ignoreCommand runs, so those tracked files were deleted
# from disk while still present in git's index. turbo-ignore's filter
# `<pkg>...[<sha>]` sets include_uncommitted, which makes turbo additionally run
# `git ls-files --others --modified` — and a tracked file deleted without
# `git rm` reports as modified. Every affected package therefore looked "changed"
# on every single build, so colossus, dcs, npracing-v1 and npracing-v3 rebuilt on
# every push regardless of what the commit touched (24 confirmed needless builds
# in six commits). Sites with no tracked PNG inside their own package dir
# (dj-fox-electrical, dch-automotive, mad-graphics) correctly skipped throughout,
# which is what isolated the cause.
#
# The rule also stripped those PNGs from the production build output: DCS's
# og:image 404'd (breaking every link preview) and the npracing sites shipped no
# icon.png/apple-icon.png, while sibling .svg/.ico files in the same directories
# served fine.
#
# It was never load-bearing anyway: 101 of the 118 tracked PNGs live under
# `output`, which is already excluded wholesale above. Do not re-add a bare
# `*.png`. Any new pattern here MUST match zero git-tracked files — enforced by
# tools/__tests__/vercel-ignore-tracked-files.test.ts.
